# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EDA tool working directories (Cadence) -- IGNORED WHOLESALE
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# genus = synthesis, innovus = place & route, signoff_mp = Pegasus DRC/LVS,
# cpf = Common Power Format, xcelium = simulation, .cadence = session state.
#
# 2026-08-27 (owner decision).  These trees are ignored WHOLESALE again and
# untracked from git.  They hold roughly 450 GB of generated output plus the
# hand-written flow scripts; the 2026-08-25 default-deny allow-list that
# re-included the scripts (93da38c) is reverted here at the owner's request.
# The scripts stay on disk -- this is a publication decision, not a deletion.
#
# Consequence to know: git is no longer the backup for genus/, innovus/,
# signoff_mp/ and cpf/ sources.  A fresh clone cannot rebuild any flow.
#
# .bazelignore still names all four trees and MUST keep doing so: tracking a
# file in git and hiding it from bazel are independent concerns.
genus/
innovus/
signoff_mp/
cpf/


.cadence/
# std_cells/ (PDK-derived .lef under foundry NDA), hardware/ (VHDL sources --
# superseded by hdl/), .claude/skills/ (local skill defs) -- untracked from git
# 2026-07-18, stay on disk only.
std_cells/
hardware/
.claude/skills/

# software/course/ (2026-08-27, owner decision): the 21 teaching labs
# (skeleton + reference), the course SDK and the .divcheck harness. 140 files.
# Untracked, still on disk -- `bazel test //software/course/...` still runs
# here, it just no longer runs in CI, which builds from a clone. Nothing
# outside the tree ever depended on it: no BUILD.bazel outside
# software/course/ names a //software/course target.
software/course/
# Pegasus/Calibre DRC-LVS run logs:
ic_bad/
# logo/ contained *.gds:
logo/
# NOTE: xcelium/ is intentionally NOT blanket-ignored. It is handled by the
#       "XCELIUM SIMULATION SOURCES" whitelist at the bottom of this file, which
#       tracks run scripts / test lists / testbenches and drops all sim artifacts.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FOUNDRY / PDK IP — NEVER commit. TSMC (and any foundry) PDK data is under NDA.
# Layout, timing, netlist, and tech files embed foundry-proprietary information.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.gds
*.gds2
*.oas
*.lef
*.def
*.def.gz
*.sdf
*.spef
*.cdl
*.oa
*.lvs.v
*.route.gz
# any file whose name carries the foundry/PDK name:
*tsmc*

# Generic EDA/simulation intermediates (in case tools run elsewhere)
*.rcf
# K2 EXCEPTION (2026-08-03), one file: the CANONICAL copy of the boot ROM image
# under tools/cosim/gate/. It is the exact byte stream both sides of the
# COSIM_BOOT lockstep execute (the reference from pc=0, the behavioural ROM
# model by hardcoded path), so a silent change to it is a silent change to the
# four pinned gate numbers. Its live copy, software/bootrom_mp/bin/rom.rcf, is
# excluded by the `software/*/bin/` DIRECTORY rule below and STAYS excluded —
# this negation covers only the record under tools/cosim/gate/.
# NOTE why a negation is legal HERE and is not for the gate files under
# xcelium/: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded, and
# `xcelium/` is a directory rule. `*.rcf` is a file-name rule and tools/cosim/
# is not excluded, so the negation takes effect normally.
!tools/cosim/gate/*.rcf
*.trn
*.dsn
*.pak
*.svcf
*.diag
INCA_libs/
xcelium.d/
*.shm/
.simvision/
xrun.log
xrun.history
xrun.key

